# Documents TOC panel UI refactor

## Goal
Refactor the Documents sidebar from pill buttons to a table-of-contents tree:
- Group `DB Schema — …` documents under a collapsible **DB Schema** folder; show child titles without the prefix.
- Move entity ref (N####) into a hover tooltip with last-edited date and editor name (multiline).
- Track `updated_by_id` on documents so “by whom” is available going forward.

## Scope
- `DocumentsToc` component + CSS (wiki-toc-style rows)
- `project_documents.updated_by_id` migration + API enrichment
- Wire into `ProjectDetailPage` documents tab

## QA follow-ups
- Removed visible “New document title” label; input + Create moved into a separate card above the TOC card (placeholder + aria-label for accessibility).
- Input placeholder shortened to “Title”.
- Fixed Kanban/image board list APIs omitting `number` (Bundefined/Mundefined); columns exist in DB since migration 0019.
